# Policy Exception Governance & Risk Evaluation Process

**Organization:** AetherPay Inc.  
**Process Owner:** Governance, Risk, and Compliance (GRC)  

---

## 1. Process Overview
AetherPay recognizes that rigid security policies can occasionally conflict with critical business operations or legacy technical dependencies. The **Policy Exception Process** provides a transparent, risk-evaluated pathway to grant temporary, time-bound policy workarounds without compromising enterprise security baselines.

---

## 2. Governance Lifecycle Workflow
[ Business Request ]  ---> Submits formal Exception Form detailing business justification
│
▼
[ Initial GRC Review] ---> GRC validates request scope, evaluates risk, and checks baseline
│
▼
[ Compensating Controls] -> Requester & GRC define mandatory risk-mitigating controls
│
▼
[ Escalation / Approval] -> Approvals required based on Residual Risk Level:
• Low/Medium Risk  --> GRC Lead Approval
• High Risk        --> CISO & VP Approval
│
▼
[ Expiration & Renewal] -> Maximum duration: 90 Days. Auto-expires unless formal renewal submitted
│
▼
[ Validation & Sunset] ---> GRC verifies permanent fix at expiration; closes exception
---

## 3. Approval Authority Matrix

| Residual Risk Level | Maximum Exception Duration | Required Approval Sign-Off |
| :---: | :---: | :--- |
| **LOW (1 – 6)** | Up to 180 Days | GRC Lead |
| **MEDIUM (8 – 12)** | Up to 90 Days | Head of Information Security / GRC Manager |
| **HIGH (15 – 25)** | Up to 30 Days | Chief Information Security Officer (CISO) & VP of Engineering |

---

## 4. Mandatory Exception Requirements
1. **Business Justification:** Exceptions are not granted for inconvenience or missed deadlines; clear business/financial impact must be demonstrated.
2. **Compensating Controls:** Every approved exception **must** feature at least one compensating control that reduces likelihood or impact.
3. **Hard Expiration Date:** Permanent exceptions are prohibited. All exceptions feature a strict expiration date requiring remediation verification.
